The six-variable cover of `SmoothedOctagon.Certificates.SmallerShort`, proved by reflection:
`B₀` (rounded outward to the fixed-point box `rootBox`) is split by `rootTop` into 1291 parts,
excluded in the modules `SmoothedOctagon.Interval.SmallerShort.Cnnn` by certificates of the
checker `SmoothedOctagon.Interval.check` (337399 leaves in all: natural, slope and LP-weight
enclosures, and contraction cuts), each chunk run by `decide +kernel` in its own declaration.

## The touching point

Numerically, `B₀` contains the point
`x° ≈ (r, δ, α, ρ, v, E) = (0.3196127, 0.0509350, 1.1397991, 0.1021522, 0.7825397, 0.1008571)`
at which `f₀, f₂, f₁₁, f₁₂` vanish simultaneously (to `10⁻¹⁴`; SLSQP maximisation of
`minᵢ fᵢ`), all of `f₀, …, f₂₂` are `≥ 0` and `f₂₃, …, f₂₆ > 0`. Only `f₂₇ = -excess ≈ -1.3·10⁻³`
excludes it: the cover needs the arctan residual, and most of the certificate lies in a
neighbourhood of `x°`.

## Main API

`certSmallerShort : SmoothedOctagon.Certificates.CertSmallerShort`.
-/

